    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>In 744 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a>–Karluk alliance destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basmyls">Basmyls</a> who had taken the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Göktürk</a> capital, and Kutlug I Bilge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">Khagan</a> claimed supreme rule over all the tribes from a new capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ordu-baliq">Ordu-Baliq</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> horsemen helped the Tang retake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a>'s rebels in 757 and again in 762, looting Luoyang each time and extracting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, titles, a fixed horse trade and royal marriages.</li><li>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogu-qaghan">Bögü Qaghan</a>'s conversion in 762 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manichaeism">Manichaeism</a> became the official religion, binding the khaganate to the Sogdian merchants who ran its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> trade.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 762 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghurs</a> sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> burnt down the Buddhist temples in which the people had taken refuge, killing more than 10,000; the Tang then paid 100,000 pieces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> to make their allies leave.</p></aside>
    </section>

